{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102295","id":2310861569,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6JvPMB","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102295","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102295.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102295.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102295","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102295/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102295/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102295/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5e614207ee928cbfa1ce0c80e2e9f787a005e845","number":102295,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add toggle state feature to Input class","user":{"login":"Saulo-de-Souza","id":17336909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzM2OTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17336909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza","html_url":"https://github.com/Saulo-de-Souza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is my first time contributing to the Godot Engine, and I noticed the lack of a built-in toggle feature for input actions. While this can be implemented in game scripts, I have added only about 10 lines of code to provide this functionality directly within the engine.\r\n\r\n**What this PR does:**\r\n- Introduces the method Input.is_action_toggled(\"action_name\"), which maintains a toggle state for an action.\r\n- The first time it is called, it returns false.\r\n- When the action is pressed (or held), it switches to true and remains true until the action is toggled again.\r\n- Works seamlessly within process or physics_process.\r\n- \r\n**Why this is useful:**\r\nThis simplifies toggle-based mechanics (such as switching a flashlight on/off) without requiring additional script logic in user projects.\r\n\r\n**Testing:**\r\n- I've verified that the toggle state updates correctly when an action is pressed.\r\n- I've confirmed that holding the button doesn't repeatedly change the state.\r\n- I've made sure that the feature doesn't interfere with existing input functions (is_action_pressed, is_action_just_pressed, etc.).\r\n\r\nI appreciate any feedback you may have on this implementation. If there's a better approach to achieving this within the existing input system, I'm open to suggestions.\r\n\r\nThank you for reviewing this PR!\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"",